For clique \(I_k\), let \(J_k\) contain only constraints supported in that clique. Its local preordering is \[T_k(g)=\left\{\sum_{
u\in\{0,1\}^{J_k}}\sigma_{k,
u}\prod_{j\in J_k}g_j^{
u_j}:\ \sigma_{k,
u}\in\Sigma[x_{I_k}]ight\}.\] The sparse preordering is \(T_{\mathrm{sp}}(g)=\sum_{k=1}^mT_k(g)\). An order-\(d\) truncation retains terms satisfying \(\deg(\sigma_{k,
u}\prod_jg_j^{
u_j})\le2d\). It is richer than the corresponding sparse quadratic module because products of distinct constraints from the same clique are permitted.
